invariant: INV-16
file: sha256.h
catches: hash_runtime_test
reason: sha256.h's sha256_on_instructions reads CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512,
  the bit of another hash's instructions. A caller that states the SHA-512
  instructions alone then runs SHA-256 on instructions it never stated,
  and one that states the SHA-256 instructions alone runs sha256.c. The
  bytes are the same either way. bin/hash_runtime_test runs every row
  under each of the 128 values the seven bits beside CH_CPU_PROBED make,
  which hold each bit with and without the other, and counts the calls
  into each path.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA512) != 0;
